From: surface-kit
Subject: Document scanning mode, full-resolution photos, refocus button

A fourth capture mode next to picture, video and QR codes. A photo taken in
it is turned into a scan of the page in the background: the page is found
(masks of the brightest area at several thresholds, of the paper's colour
at any brightness so shadows stay on the page, and of colours rare along
the border; of the outlines that are mostly filled and have real edges
the largest wins),
its four corners taken from the convex hull. A dialog shows the photo
with that outline and a handle on each corner to drag (a page on other
white paper has no edge to find); without a page it starts just inside
the frame. Save warps the page to an upright rectangle, evens out the
paper per colour channel to neutral white, and cleans it up like a
scanner, adapted to the page's measured noise (dim rooms mean high gain):
3x3 median and a 5x5 sigma filter on luma, a box on chroma, an unsharp
mask on luma for text edges, and levels with a 1.3 gamma that take paper
plus its grain to white and ink to neutral black while keeping thin lines
and coloured marks.
The photo stays next to the scan. Plain Rust and cairo, no new crates.

The adjust dialog also turns the page (an arrow marks the side that
becomes the top; the last rotation is kept for the next page), switches
to black and white (remembered in document-black-white), shows a
magnifier while a corner is dragged, and collects pages: "Add Page" keeps
the scan for a PDF, and the next page saved normally writes them all into
one PDF, with an Open button. With Tesseract installed the PDF is
searchable (German and English text layer); otherwise the JPEG pages go
in as they are.

A focus button next to the countdown, and a tap on the picture, ask the
camera to focus again: they touch $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/libcamera-af-trigger,
which the surface-kit libcamera build's autofocus watches.

The camera streamed at 1080p at most, and pictures are taken from the
stream. aperture now has stream profiles: video and QR codes keep 1080p,
picture mode takes the camera's full width at 16:9 (3200x1800 at 20 fps
on the Surface Pro 7 rear camera instead of 1920x1080), document mode
full resolution at 4:3 (3200x2400). Changing mode restarts the stream
whenever the profile changes (comparing caps missed that: other mode
changes had already put them on the filter without a restart).
